{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION #2 — \"Defect B\" does not exist. Retracting it before it reaches a change.\n\nMy previous comment listed a second defect: that `REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL` \"appears nowhere in\ninfra/\" and exists only as an operator's hand-appended .env line that fetch-secrets would wipe.\nThat is FALSE. I verified directly:\n\n  infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:351\n    REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL: \"${REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL:-https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp}\"\n  infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:360\n    -e \"REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL=${REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL:-https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp}\"\n\nBoth surfaces carry it, with the SAME non-empty default, so a blue-green container gets a valid\nissuer URL from git with no .env line at all. There is even existing coverage pinning it:\ntests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py:72-80 asserts the mcp service env defines a non-empty\nREBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL. The claim came from a faulty grep; it does not survive a direct read.\n\nConsequences for the story:\n1. The operator's 16:55Z `env_file` injection was REDUNDANT, not load-bearing. The default\n   already covered it. What actually recovered the box was the 16:45:45Z manual `fetch-secrets.sh`\n   run that rewrote mcp-static-tokens.json with 3 records; the 16:55Z `--force-recreate` merely\n   started a container that read the now-good file. The ticket's Summary attributes the recovery\n   to the env_file injection — that attribution is wrong.\n2. There is therefore NO \"un-versioned live config that will self-destruct\". fetch-secrets\n   regenerating .env without that key is harmless, because the key is not needed in .env.\n3. The stated risk that \"fixing Defect A would TRIGGER Defect B\" is void. Defect A is safe to\n   land alone.\n\nSo this ticket reduces to exactly ONE landable defect — Defect A: the mcp blue-green path\n(autodeploy.sh:621-700) never calls fetch-secrets.sh, so an SSM secret rotation never reaches a\nnew container. The review-bot path already does this correctly at autodeploy.sh:579. That single\nchange is sufficient to explain the incident and prevent recurrence: with it, the PATs populated\nat 16:42Z would have been materialized on the very next deploy instead of requiring a human.\n\nThe ticket's title and AC list still mention the un-versioned issuer fix; those ACs are dropped\nas based on a false premise. Remaining AC: the mcp deploy path refreshes SSM-sourced secrets\nbefore starting the new container, with fail-fast semantics matching the bot path."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787712611790719001,"uuid":"dd6301ac-8257-4697-982b-6b3668a8adee"}